<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Douglass returns two weeks after his intake visit and is seen by Dr. Morrison, clinical psychology, the same afternoon. He has used the diclofenac gel two or three times a day, takes a ten-minute break each hour of writing, and has bought a wide-barrel pen. The aching after an hour of writing is a little less, about 4 of 10, and the morning stiffness eases within fifteen minutes. He had his first hand-therapy session last week and is doing the exercises twice a day. The gel has caused no rash. He still sleeps about five hours on working nights, writing until after midnight and waking early; he had one nightmare about his youth in the two weeks, after which he got up and wrote for an hour. Before today&apos;s evaluation he asked what it would involve and agreed to it; he said he wants to know whether the nightmares are a disorder and what help there is for sleep. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Hand</td><td>Pain 4 of 10 after an hour of writing, down from 5; gel well tolerated; first hand-therapy session done</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About five hours on working nights; one nightmare in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Evaluation</td><td>Clinical psychology structured interview today, with his consent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Right-hand ache after long writing, less than at intake; morning stiffness under fifteen minutes; no other joint pain</td></tr><tr><td>Integumentary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No rash or irritation where the gel is applied</td></tr><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Tired on days after short sleep; no fever or weight change</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>One nightmare in two weeks; mood steady; no thoughts of suicide or self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

