    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Post-traumatic osteoarthritis of the right hand (M19.141)</content>. Early improvement with topical diclofenac, writing breaks, and the first hand-therapy session; pain 4 of 10. The intake X-ray showed healed, angulated fourth and fifth metacarpal fractures with joint-space narrowing and osteophytes at those knuckles. No validated hand-function score was taken at intake or today. [S]<list><item>Continue diclofenac gel up to four times a day.</item><item>Five more hand-therapy sessions over the next seven weeks.</item><item>FIHOA hand-function score from the next visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Personal history of psychological trauma (Z91.49)</content>. Dr. Morrison&apos;s structured interview today finds trauma-related symptoms below the threshold for PTSD: occasional nightmares and watchfulness in public, with no avoidance of reminders (he writes and speaks about his past by choice) and no lasting negative change in how he sees himself or the world. No PTSD diagnosis is made. The PCL-5 of 24 at intake agrees. [S]<list><item>No trauma-focused psychotherapy or medication now, which is his choice and fits the findings; both remain open if symptoms grow.</item><item>PCL-5 and PHQ-9 at each chronic-care review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Insufficient sleep (Z72.820)</content>. About five hours on working nights, from late writing and early waking, with an occasional nightmare. [S]<list><item>Two brief behavioral sleep sessions with Dr. Morrison, the first today: a fixed waking time, a seven-hour sleep window, no writing in the last hour before bed, and a short routine for nights after a nightmare.</item><item>Sleep diary for two weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Consent before each question, examination, and test; chaperone offered</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>He agreed to the hand examination and to the psychology evaluation after each was explained</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Hand joint examination (range of motion, swelling, alignment, grip)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Bony enlargement at the fourth and fifth knuckles; flexion reduced by about 20 degrees; grip 80 percent of the left; no inflammation</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Hand pain, 0 to 10 numeric rating</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4 of 10 after an hour of writing, down from 5</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Hand function with a validated instrument (FIHOA)</td><td>Each clinical encounter</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not given at intake or today; function was recorded only as minutes of writing before pain. No harm, because pain scores and the examination guided care. Corrective action: FIHOA added to the visit template and given from the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Hand exercise and joint-protection program</td><td>Ongoing; six hand-therapy sessions over eight weeks, then a home program</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First hand-therapy session done; exercises twice a day</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Topical NSAID tolerance (skin irritation)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No skin irritation</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>CBC, creatinine, and blood pressure for chronic oral NSAID use; ALT for chronic acetaminophen</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months, only with chronic oral NSAID or acetaminophen use</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Topical diclofenac only; no oral NSAID or regular acetaminophen</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Hand radiograph</td><td>At diagnosis; not for routine follow-up</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Intake X-ray: healed, angulated fourth and fifth metacarpal fractures with post-traumatic arthritis at those knuckles</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Clinical psychology evaluation (structured interview, CAPS-5)</td><td>Once at the start; again if symptoms rise or he wants treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dr. Morrison today: below the threshold for PTSD; no diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PCL-5 (trauma-related symptom severity)</td><td>At intake and at each chronic-care visit (measurement-based care)</td><td>Up to date</td><td>24 at intake two weeks ago, below the 31 to 33 range for probable PTSD; today&apos;s structured interview took its place; next at the ten-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 (depression, with item 9)</td><td>At intake and at each chronic-care visit; also the CMID mental-health and coping screen for osteoarthritis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>5 at intake, item 9 scored 0; next at the ten-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep hours, sleep diary, and nightmare frequency</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About five hours on working nights; one nightmare in two weeks; sleep diary started</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Brief behavioral treatment for insomnia</td><td>Two sessions, two weeks apart</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First session with Dr. Morrison today; second in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Strengths and supports he names</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>His writing and work, family and community, and faith; visits arranged around his speaking travel</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Write for an hour with right-hand pain no higher than 2 of 10. In progress; target 2026-05-19 [S]</item><item>Sleep at least seven hours on five nights a week. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>Track trauma-related symptoms with the PCL-5 and return to psychology if the score reaches the probable-PTSD range or he wants treatment. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item><item>Every examination, test, and question about his history happens only with his agreement. In progress; target 2026-08-18 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); Trauma-Informed Care in Behavioral Health Services (Treatment Improvement Protocol 57) (2014); 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis monograph (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder and Obstructive Sleep Apnea (2025); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Second sleep session with Dr. Morrison in two weeks. Ten-week review after the hand-therapy course, with the PCL-5, PHQ-9, and FIHOA. Next scheduled visit 2026-05-19: ten-week review after hand therapy and two sleep sessions. [S]</paragraph></text>

